=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTED_VALUE_HARDCODED
issue: 471
title: a producer imported from one module lends nothing for a same-named class changed in a sibling module
origin: ruling 471 Q1 (c), the producer resolved through the fixture file's own imports: the conftest
origin2: imports Provider from shop.a, and the diff changes shop.b.Provider. The changed module is not
origin3: reachable from shop.a (THREATMODEL row 35's same-package collision, D-046), so both findings
origin4: block. The test file imports nothing, so EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED has no package credit either.
=== before: shop/b.py ===
class Provider:
    @property
    def default_voice(self):
        return "rachel"
=== after: shop/b.py ===
class Provider:
    @property
    def default_voice(self):
        return "matilda"
=== before: tests/test_voices.py ===
def test_default_voice(provider):
    assert provider.default_voice == "rachel"
=== after: tests/test_voices.py ===
def test_default_voice(provider):
    assert provider.default_voice == "matilda"
=== head: shop/a.py ===
class Provider:
    @property
    def default_voice(self):
        return "rachel"
=== head: tests/conftest.py ===
import pytest

from shop.a import Provider


@pytest.fixture
def provider():
    return Provider()
